# MediaTek WLAN (MT6627 on CONSYS, AHB/PDMA host interface).

config MTK_WCN_WLAN
	tristate "MediaTek WCN WLAN driver"
	depends on MTK_WCN_WMT
	depends on CFG80211
	depends on ARCH_MEDIATEK || COMPILE_TEST
	select CRC32
	select FW_LOADER
	help
	  Host driver for the MediaTek WLAN function embedded in the
	  connectivity subsystem (MT6628/MT6627 gen2, AHB host interface
	  with optional AP-DMA).  It owns the AHB host interface, the
	  firmware download path and the WMT function power sequencing, and
	  exposes one cfg80211 station interface plus its Ethernet netdev.

	  Supported feature set, and nothing beyond it:

	  - station (infrastructure) mode on 2.4 GHz channels 1 to 14,
	    legacy rates only, no 5 GHz band;
	  - open (no encryption) networks only.  There is no key offload,
	    so WPA/WPA2/802.1X association requests are rejected with
	    -EOPNOTSUPP instead of associating unencrypted;
	  - software scan: probe requests are built by the host and sent
	    through the HIF, beacons and probe responses received from the
	    HIF are reported to cfg80211.  Passive scans send no frames;
	  - no AP, IBSS, mesh, P2P or monitor interface, no hardware scan,
	    no scheduled scan, no remain-on-channel and no WoWLAN.

	  The interface is controlled through cfg80211 only (iw,
	  wpa_supplicant); the driver registers no private character
	  device or ioctl ABI.

	  Building without CONFIG_RFKILL is supported; the rfkill switch is
	  then simply absent and WLAN is controlled through WMT.

	  The module is called mtk_wcn_wlan.
